'' 'x = type( ... )' INTO EVERY KIND OF STORAGE. The branch that writes a field list
'' straight into its destination asked LocalFor for a SLOT, and LocalFor MAKES one for
'' any symbol: a SHARED 'eyepoint = type( 512, 384, 800 )' filled a fresh local nobody
'' reads and left the global zero (starshine.bas's planet collapsed to the origin), a
'' BYREF parameter had the fields written across the reference (a segfault), and a
'' STATIC lost them too. A FIELD or ELEMENT target, and a qualified 'ns.v', fell to the
'' plain store instead and wrote the literal's INTEGER bits into single fields:
'' 'arr( 0 ) = type( 5, 6, 7 )' read back 7.0e-45.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 running the source -- and tiko's build prints the same:
'' see the header of src/type-literal-assign-target.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/type-literal-assign-target.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-NOT: local agg sh size
'' EXPECT-NOT: local agg st size
'' GOLDEN: expected/type-literal-assign-target.out
